<div class="p5-section">

    <div class="p5-section-label">Phase 5 · Complete System Retrofit</div>
    <h2 class="p5-section-title">Dual-rail steam → rotary wheels → transmission → vehicle drive</h2>
    <p class="p5-section-lead">
        Phase 5 is a complete departure from traditional piston architecture. Two parallel
        rails (left and right) are driven simultaneously by steam pressure from a central
        reservoir. These rails power dual rotary converter wheels mounted on the engine
        block (like external steam-engine wheels). As the converter wheels rotate, their
        lobes engage follower pistons within an integrated transmission chamber. Piston
        motion drives the main crankshaft. A pressure-regulating system keeps tank
        pressure proportional to throttle input and instantaneous engine RPM demand.
        Dual batteries provide primary and backup electrical power to the PCW (Pressure
        Control Unit) and heating systems. This creates a self-regulating, efficiency-driven
        power plant with zero combustion contamination.
    </p>

