                <li><strong>Thermostat setpoint:</strong> 220°C (428°F, full saturation)</li>
                <li><strong>Water feed:</strong> Condensed exhaust from transmission chamber</li>
                <li><strong>Duty cycle:</strong> Pulse-width modulated by PCW to maintain constant steam quality</li>
                <li><strong>Protection:</strong> Thermostatic relief, low-water shutoff (float sensor)</li>
                <li><strong>Warm-up time:</strong> ~45–60 seconds to operating pressure</li>
                <li><strong>Continuous energy input:</strong> Alternator must supply ≥ 5 kW; Battery A supplies gap during idle</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ===================================================
             SECTION: PRESSURE-RPM LOAD-FOLLOWING CURVE
             ===================================================== -->
    <hr class="p5-sep" />
    <div class="p5-section-label">Control Strategy</div>
    <h2 class="p5-section-title">Pressure-RPM load-following dynamics</h2>
    <p class="p5-section-lead">
        The core innovation of Phase 5 is its dynamic pressure regulation. Unlike conventional
        throttle systems that modulate fuel flow, the PCW adjusts pressure relief valve opening
        proportionally to both throttle position and instantaneous engine RPM. This creates a
        smooth, predictable power delivery that never exceeds tank safety limits.
    </p>

