            adjusts relief valve to keep the system operating on the active throttle curve. At 100% throttle,
            pressure reaches maximum (150 PSI) and levels off—preventing tank over-pressure. Lower throttle
            settings produce lower pressure curves, reducing power output and fuel (steam) consumption.
            This load-following characteristic provides smooth, predictable acceleration without throttle lag.
        </p>
