    <h2 class="p5-section-title">Phase 5 output specifications and efficiency calculations</h2>

    <div class="p5-performance-grid">
        <div class="p5-performance-card">
            <h3>Maximum Power Output</h3>
            <div class="p5-calc-block">
                <p><strong>At rated conditions (100 PSI, 3000 RPM):</strong></p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Force per rail: F = P × A = 100 PSI × 50.27 in² ≈ 5,027 lbf</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Torque per cycle: τ = 5,027 × 2 in ≈ 10,054 in-lbf ≈ 837 ft-lbf</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Cycles per minute: 3,000 RPM / 2 = 1,500 power strokes/min</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Power = (837 ft-lbf × 1,500) / 5,252 ≈ <strong>238 hp</strong></p>
                <p style="margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 11px; color: #7a9ab0; font-style: italic;">
                    (Both rails firing; transmission efficiency ~92%; net output ≈ 219 hp to wheels)
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-performance-card">
            <h3>Thermal Efficiency</h3>
            <div class="p5-calc-block">
                <p><strong>Rankine cycle theoretical efficiency:</strong></p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">η_th = 1 − (T_c / T_h) = 1 − (373 K / 473 K) ≈ 21.1%</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">(T_h = 200°C boiler; T_c = 100°C condenser)</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;"><strong>Real-world Phase 5 (estimated):</strong> 18–20% (includes valve, bearing, seal losses)</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Steam energy input  100 PSI: ~250 BTU/lbm per cycle</p>
                <p style="margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 11px; color: #7a9ab0; font-style: italic;">
                    (Significantly better than Otto cycle petrol engines at 25–35% peak, comparable to diesel at 30–40%)
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-performance-card">
            <h3>Fuel Consumption (Water/Steam)</h3>
            <div class="p5-calc-block">
                <p><strong>At 50% throttle, 3000 RPM (highway cruising):</strong></p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Operating pressure: 75 PSI</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Power output: ~110 hp</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Steam flow rate: Q = 2 cylinders × 604 cm³ × 50 Hz = 60.4 L/s</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Water consumption: 60.4 L/s ≈ 950 gal/hr (at full power)</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">At 50% throttle: ~475 gal/hr or ~1.32 gal/mile (for reference vehicle)</p>
                <p style="margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 11px; color: #7a9ab0; font-style: italic;">
                    (Condensate recovery loop recycles ~85% water; net top-up ~0.2 gal/mile during normal highway driving)
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-performance-card">
            <h3>Electrical Energy Balance</h3>
            <div class="p5-calc-block">
                <p><strong>Energy flow at cruising (50% throttle, 3000 RPM):</strong></p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Mechanical power input: 110 hp ≈ 82 kW</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Heating duty (steam generation): 4.5 kW (from Battery A)</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Alternator output (net): ~3 kW  3000 RPM</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Battery A draw: 4.5 − 3.0 = 1.5 kW deficit during cruise</p>
                <p style="margin: 0.5rem 0;">Battery autonomy  1.5 kW drain: 4.8 kWh / 1.5 kW ≈ 3.2 hours (or ~150 miles highway range)</p>
                <p style="margin-top: 0.8rem; font-size: 11px; color: #7a9ab0; font-style: italic;">
                    (Actual range depends on driving cycle; urban stop-and-go drains faster; highway stretches benefit from high alternator output)
                </p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <!-- ===================================================
             SECTION: SAFETY SYSTEMS
             ===================================================== -->
    <hr class="p5-sep" />
    <div class="p5-section-label">Safety & Redundancy</div>
    <h2 class="p5-section-title">Multi-layer protection and failure isolation</h2>

    <div class="p5-safety-grid">
        <div class="p5-safety-card critical">
            <div class="p5-safety-tag">CRITICAL</div>
            <h4>Primary Pressure Relief (Hard Line)</h4>
            <p>
                Mechanical spring-loaded relief valve set to 165 PSI. <strong>Not computer-controlled.</strong>
                Pops open if tank pressure exceeds setpoint, regardless of PCW state. Protects against ASME
                vessel code violations. Flow capacity: 80 L/min. Prevents catastrophic rupture.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-safety-card critical">
            <div class="p5-safety-tag">CRITICAL</div>
            <h4>Low-Water Shutoff (Float Sensor)</h4>
            <p>
                Mechanical float in condenser tank. If water level drops below 15% (insufficient steam
                generation), relay cuts power to boiler heater and pressurizes tank vent line (safe depressurization).
                Engine coasts to stop. Prevents dry-run damage and superheater scaling.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-safety-card major">
            <div class="p5-safety-tag">MAJOR</div>
            <h4>Battery Voltage Monitoring</h4>
            <p>
                PCW monitors Battery A voltage every 10 ms. If voltage drops below 10.5 V for &gt;100 ms,
                automatic switchover to Battery B via diode-OR isolation circuit. LED indicator on dash alerts driver.
                Battery B provides 30–45 minutes continued operation at reduced heating power.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-safety-card major">
            <div class="p5-safety-tag">MAJOR</div>
            <h4>Over-Temperature Shutdown</h4>
            <p>
                Boiler thermostat set to 230°C. If temperature exceeds setpoint, heating element relay opens.
                PCW simultaneously cuts pressure relief solenoid power, allowing tank to depressurize through vent.
                Driver receives audible alarm. Prevents boiler steam quality degradation and scaling.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-safety-card design">
            <div class="p5-safety-tag">DESIGN</div>
            <h4>PCW Failsafe (Lose-Pressure Architecture)</h4>
            <p>
                If PCW power is lost or microcontroller crashes, the proportional relief valve spring-biases
                to a safe de-energized state (partially open, ~50 PSI regulation). Engine idles safely; no
                runaway condition. Driver can limp home on Battery B + manual engine kill switch.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="p5-safety-card design">
            <div class="p5-safety-tag">DESIGN</div>
            <h4>Condensate Filtration & Demineralization</h4>
            <p>
                Inline cartridge filter (10 micron) removes corrosion debris. Demineralizer cartridge prevents
                mineral scale buildup in boiler tubes (hard water ions exchanged for H⁺). Annual cartridge replacement
                (~$30). Extends boiler life 3–5× compared to untreated water.
            </p>
        </div>
    </div>

